course: dictionary
lesson: 6439
title: A word from the Aztecs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words came into English from other languages, and their history can tell you a lot. The word nahuatl is the name of a language. «Many Indigenous languages are still spoken, such as Quechua by several million people in the Andes, Guaraní in Paraguay and Nahuatl in Mexico.» The sentence tells you that Nahuatl is still spoken today, in Mexico.
explain: Indigenous means belonging to the people who first lived in a place. The Andes and Mexico were home to Indigenous peoples long before Europeans arrived. The context clues show you that Nahuatl is a living language, not just a word from a history book.
explain: Nahuatl is the language of the Aztecs. Lots of English words come from it, such as chocolate, tomato, avocado and chilli. When you meet a word from another language, ask: where did this word come from, and what did it mean there?
fact: Nahuatl is the language of the Aztecs.
fact: Nahuatl is still spoken today by over a million people in Mexico.
fact: English words like chocolate, tomato, avocado and chilli come from Nahuatl.
fact: Indigenous means belonging to the first people who lived in a place.
fact: Words that come from another language are called loan words.
exercise: «Many Indigenous languages are still spoken, such as Quechua, Guaraní and Nahuatl.» In which country is Nahuatl spoken? | Paraguay | Peru | *Mexico | Scotland
exercise: Which of these English words comes from Nahuatl? | Hamburger | Pizza | Spaghetti | *Tomato
exercise: In the word list, nahuatl is a noun. What is it the name of? | *A language | A country | A food | An Aztec king
test: About how many people still speak Nahuatl today? | *Over a million | Over a hundred | Only ten | None at all
test: Which word names the language of the Aztecs? | *Nahuatl | Quechua | Mexico | Chilli
exam: Why is Nahuatl important for English speakers? | *It gave English words like chocolate and chilli | It is an English word that means food | It is the language of Paraguay | It was invented only last year
